        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1406">

                <pb facs="0930" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg814"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/271.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Spanish Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 263.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 19, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 12th instant concerning the dangers apprehended by
                    the Spanish colony in the port of Guaymas in case the town should be taken by
                    the revolutionary party. You request that instructions may be issued to the
                    consular officer of the United States at Guaymas to protect the Spanish subjects
                    above mentioned in case it should prove necessary.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to say in reply that-according to information received by the
                    Department its consular agent at Guaymas is now in the United States and there
                    is at present no representative of this Department in Guaymas. In these
                    circumstances the Department has communicated a copy of your note to the
                    Secretary of the Navy and has asked him to issue orders to the American naval
                    commander in the waters about Guaymas to extend all practicable and proper
                    protection to the Spanish subjects in that town in case necessity for such
                    protection should arise.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
